join Zanele (Neutral) left
join Hope (Neutral) right
Zanele: Eleven years I have taught in this village, and he is the first one to leave for something better rather than for work.
Zanele: That is the whole point of it. I want to be clear that I know that.
- It's still hard
	Hope: It's still hard.
	Zanele: It is very hard, and it is exactly what was supposed to happen, and I would not change one part of it.
	Zanele: He left the physics textbook. The rained-on one, with the missing diagrams.
	Zanele: He told you it was for whoever is next.
Zanele: She has been ahead of the class since March. She has not mentioned it to anyone, which is how I know she is not doing it for attention.
Zanele: It will be four or five years before it matters. That is all right. I have four or five years.
